@startuml bootwire_stale_response_sequence
!include ../_style.iuml
title <size:21><color:#1B3A5F><b>Fault: Late Response</b></color></size>\n<size:13><color:#5B6B7C>a reply to an older request carries another SEQ and is ignored</color></size>
!include _participants.iuml

autonumber "<b>00"
APP -> HOST : erase(block)
HOST -> TP : ERASE [SEQ=0x80, …]
activate TP
TP -> BL : erase the block (slow part)
... erase_timeout passes before the answer ...
HOST -> TP : ERASE [SEQ=0x80, …]  <color:#1E90D6><b>«resend, waits in the target RX»</b></color>
BL --> TP : done
TP --> HOST : [SEQ=0x80, 0x90, <color:#1E8449><b>OK</b></color>]
deactivate TP
HOST --> APP : return
APP -> HOST : write(chunk)
HOST -> HOST : flush RX, SEQ = 0x81
activate TP
TP -> TP : the resend is handled now:\n(0x80, ERASE) = cached key
TP --> HOST : [SEQ=0x80, 0x90, <color:#1E8449><b>OK</b></color>]  <color:#1E90D6><b>«replay arrives late»</b></color>
deactivate TP
HOST -> TP : WRITE [SEQ=0x81, …]
HOST -> HOST : SEQ 0x80 ≠ 0x81 → ignore
activate TP
TP -> BL : program + read back
TP --> HOST : [SEQ=0x81, 0x91, <color:#1E8449><b>OK</b></color>]
deactivate TP
HOST --> APP : return
note over HOST, TP
  The host accepts a response only when both SEQ and CMD match the request
  it is waiting for. Late copies of older answers are harmless.
end note
@enduml
